# gantry-snapshotter-node-config - the agent that owns the node's containerd
# configuration.
#
# containerd will not talk to a snapshotter it has not been told about, and
# there is no API for telling it at runtime: the proxy plugin, the runtime
# handler and the CRI default all live in /etc/containerd/config.toml and take
# effect on restart. Something has to edit that file on every node, and this is
# it. Doing it by hand is possible and is what the README describes, but it is
# an ordering-sensitive edit repeated per node and then repeated again every
# time a node is reimaged, which is exactly the kind of thing that is wrong
# once and then wrong forever.
#
# Notes, all of them load bearing:
#
#   - There is deliberately no runtimeClassName here, which is the opposite of
#     the snapshotter's own DaemonSet. It cannot use gantry-bootstrap, because
#     the handler that name refers to is what this pod creates. On a fresh node
#     that is fine: containerd is unmodified and the default handler works. On a
#     node that is already fully configured and has just rebooted, containerd's
#     default snapshotter is gantry and the socket is gone with the tmpfs, so
#     this pod cannot start until the snapshotter's pod - which can, because it
#     has the bootstrap handler - is serving again. That wait is not a deadlock,
#     and there is nothing for this pod to do on such a node until then anyway.
#
#   - hostPID plus privileged, because restarting containerd means entering the
#     host's namespaces with nsenter and asking systemd. There is no way to
#     restart a host service from a container without being able to become the
#     host.
#
#   - Restarting containerd does not stop running containers. Their shims are
#     separate processes that outlive containerd and reattach when it comes
#     back. What does stall is anything that needs the CRI socket, so the
#     restart is only issued when the merge actually changed something.
#
#   - The merge is on the parsed TOML document, not on the text, and only the
#     keys it owns are touched. A node's own installer already owns that file -
#     on AKS it pins the pause image, the registry config path and runc's cgroup
#     driver - so overwriting it with a rendered copy breaks the node. The
#     original is backed up once to config.toml.gantry-orig.
#
#   - nodeSelector racer.unbounded-cloud.io/active. The snapshotter is only
#     useful on a node running racer, and pointing containerd at a snapshotter
#     that will never be scheduled there is how a node stops being able to start
#     pods. Gating both DaemonSets on the same label keeps the configuration and
#     the agent on exactly the same set of nodes.
#
#   - The loop never exits. It re-checks on a timer so that a node whose
#     configuration is rewritten underneath it - by a package upgrade, by a
#     reimage, by an operator - is brought back without anyone noticing.
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: DaemonSet
metadata:
  name: gantry-snapshotter-node-config
  namespace: {{ default "unbounded-system" .Namespace }}
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: gantry-snapshotter
    app.kubernetes.io/component: node-config
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app.kubernetes.io/name: gantry-snapshotter
      app.kubernetes.io/component: node-config
  updateStrategy:
    type: RollingUpdate
    rollingUpdate:
      # This pod restarts containerd. Rolling it across the whole cluster at
      # once would stall pod creation everywhere at once.
      maxUnavailable: 1
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/name: gantry-snapshotter
        app.kubernetes.io/component: node-config
    spec:
      serviceAccountName: gantry-snapshotter
      # Entering the host's namespaces to restart containerd needs to see PID 1.
      hostPID: true
      hostNetwork: false
      dnsPolicy: ClusterFirst
      priorityClassName: gantry-snapshotter-node-critical
      tolerations:
        - operator: Exists
      nodeSelector:
        racer.unbounded-cloud.io/active: "true"
      # Long enough for the shutdown revert to rewrite the configuration and
      # wait for containerd to come back. A pod killed before it finishes
      # leaves the node on the snapshotter with nothing watching it.
      terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 180
      containers:
        - name: node-config
          image: {{ .Image }}
          imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
          args:
            - node-config
            - --config=/host/etc/containerd/config.toml
            - --socket=/run/gantry-snapshotter/snapshotter.sock
            - --containerd-socket=/run/containerd/containerd.sock
            - --platform={{ .Platform | default "linux/amd64" }}
            # How long the snapshotter's socket may stay silent before the
            # node drops back to overlayfs. Long enough to ride out a restart
            # of the snapshotter, short enough that a node whose snapshotter
            # has genuinely gone can pull images again without help.
            - --revert-after=90s
            - --interval=15s
          securityContext:
            privileged: true
            runAsUser: 0
            runAsGroup: 0
            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
            seccompProfile:
              type: RuntimeDefault
          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: 10m
              memory: 32Mi
            limits:
              memory: 128Mi
          volumeMounts:
            # Mounted at /host/etc/containerd rather than /etc/containerd so
            # that a bug in this agent cannot rewrite its own image's /etc.
            - name: containerd-config
              mountPath: /host/etc/containerd
            # Watched, not created: this is how the agent knows the
            # snapshotter is actually serving before it makes it the default.
            - name: snapshotter-run
              mountPath: /run/gantry-snapshotter
              readOnly: true
            - name: containerd-run
              mountPath: /run/containerd
              readOnly: true
      volumes:
        - name: containerd-config
          hostPath:
            path: /etc/containerd
            type: Directory
        - name: snapshotter-run
          hostPath:
            path: /run/gantry-snapshotter
            type: DirectoryOrCreate
        - name: containerd-run
          hostPath:
            path: /run/containerd
            type: Directory
